# Agent-Native SDLC

The AI-native software lifecycle for **Cursor, GitHub Copilot, Codex, Gemini
CLI, Aider and any agent that reads `AGENTS.md`**. Each stage reads the
artifact the previous stage committed and commits its own; together they are
the audit trail. Humans sit at the gates between stages, not inside every step.

```
request ──▶ 1 SPEC ──▶ 2 BUILD ──▶ 3 TEST ──▶ 4 DEPLOY ──▶ 5 MAINTAIN ──┐
             spec.md    plan.md     green      review.md     finding     │
             ▲                                                            │
             └────────────────────── new spec ◀───────────────────────────┘
```

> **This repository is generated.** It is built from
> [{{source_repo}}](https://github.com/{{source_repo}}) — the Claude Code
> version — and synced on every change there. Version {{version}}, source
> commit `{{source_commit}}`. Open issues and pull requests on the source
> repository; changes made here are overwritten.
>
> **Using Claude Code?** Install [ai-native-sdlc](https://github.com/{{source_repo}})
> instead. It runs the same lifecycle with more: stage skills that load on
> demand, parallel review subagents, and hooks that can ask a model.

