## Install

```bash
git clone https://github.com/{{mirror_repo}}.git
python3 agent-native-sdlc/install.py /path/to/your/repo
```

The installer detects which agents the repository uses and installs what each
one reads. Name them explicitly with `--agents cursor,copilot`, or preview with
`--dry-run`. It merges rather than overwrites — an existing `AGENTS.md`,
`.cursor/hooks.json` or Gemini settings keep their contents — and re-running it
is how you update.

Then open the repository with your agent and say:

> set up the SDLC

It follows `.sdlc/playbook/setup.md`: reads the repo, fills in `AGENTS.md`,
tailors the guards, and lists every decision still open.

**Requirements:** Python 3.9+ and git. The guards are bash scripts; on Windows
they need `bash` on the path, which Git for Windows provides.

---

## What each agent gets

| Agent | Lifecycle instructions | Stage rules on demand | Guard hooks | Spec gate in CI |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| **Cursor** | `AGENTS.md` | `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` | `.cursor/hooks.json` | ✓ |
| **GitHub Copilot** — VS Code, CLI, cloud agent | `AGENTS.md` | `.github/instructions/` | `.github/hooks/sdlc.json` | ✓ |
| **Gemini CLI** | `AGENTS.md`, via `.gemini/settings.json` | through `AGENTS.md` | — | ✓ |
| **Aider** | `AGENTS.md`, via `.aider.conf.yml` | through `AGENTS.md` | — | ✓ |
| **Codex, Jules, Zed, Windsurf, Devin, Amp, Junie, opencode** and other `AGENTS.md` readers | `AGENTS.md` | through `AGENTS.md` | — | ✓ |

"Through `AGENTS.md`" means the lifecycle block names the playbook file for
each stage and tells the agent to read it before acting — every agent gets
the procedures, the ones without conditional rules just get them by reference.

The last column is the one that matters most. The **spec gate** runs in CI,
not inside an agent: a pull request that changes code without an approved
spec and plan fails, whichever tool wrote it. Make the check required in branch
protection and it binds every agent — including ones not on this list — and
every person.

