## The five stages

| # | Stage | Playbook | Produces |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | Spec | `.sdlc/playbook/1-spec.md` | `.sdlc/<slug>/spec.md` |
| 2 | Build | `.sdlc/playbook/2-build.md` | `.sdlc/<slug>/plan.md`, then code |
| 3 | Test | `.sdlc/playbook/3-test.md` | Green tests, build, lint |
| 4 | Deploy | `.sdlc/playbook/4-deploy.md` | `.sdlc/<slug>/review.md`, a merged PR |
| 5 | Maintain | `.sdlc/playbook/5-maintain.md` | A finding, promoted to a new spec |

Routing, gate owners and autonomy tiers are in `.sdlc/playbook/README.md`.
Review passes — bugs, security, spec conformance — are in
`.sdlc/playbook/review-passes/`.

## The rules that do not bend

- **Nothing is built without an approved spec.** Nothing is coded without an
  accepted plan. CI enforces it.
- **The agent never approves its own work.** It writes, it reviews other
  changes, a human approves.
- **Production requires a named human authorization**, enforced by a guard.
- **Tests are never weakened to go green.** For bugs: failing test first,
  committed on its own, then the fix.
- **Findings loop back as specs**, never as silent patches.

